thanks to its beginnings is a  best-selling book World War Z seems  destined for box office glory someday  but that road to the big screen wasn't  always an easy one we're taking a look  back at the ending of World War Z and  how it got from prized source material  to hailed script to problem production  to box office head after the success of  his 2003 how-to manual the zombie  survival guide author Max Brooks decided  to take his love of The Walking Dead up  a notch his next book was a harrowing  oral history style novel said in the era  after the outbreak of a virus that  reanimates corpses and nearly wipes out  the human race in it a member of the UN  post-war commission travels to locations  around the world conducting interviews  to take the reader from the first  hotspots to the collapse of society to  the darkest moments when humanity finds  a way to fight back audiences responded  with great enthusiasm and World War Z  would top the New York Times bestseller  list eventually selling more than a  million copies with that level of  success it was only a matter of time  before Hollywood came calling and Brad  Pitt's company Plan B eventually landed  the rights Pitt brought on J michael  Straczynski a veteran genre writer  behind cult classics like Babylon 5 to  craft the first draft of the script  Straczynski version kept the interview  format of the book intact and his draft  was strong enough to attract director  Marc Forster to the project it was here  that the first signs of trouble in the  making of the film began to emerge fresh  off is James Bond film Quantum of Solace  Foresters ideas for World War Z clashed  with stress in skis and the director  asked for rewrites state of play writer  Matthew Michael Carnahan was brought in  to develop a new more action heavy  script and major changes were made  instead of focusing on the aftermath of  the war with the zombies the new script  placed Pitt's character Jerry Lane in  the middle of the outbreak from the  beginning Carnahan's  script was solid enough that shooting  could begin but studio executives still  weren't sure about the film's ending in  Carnahan's version of the story pits  Jerry Lane would endure everything from  a crash landing in Russia to a time jump  to an invasion  the west coast of the United States all  without ever reuniting with his family  eventually it was decided that rewrites  and reshoots were needed to get the film  and ship lost writer damon lindelof and  later the martian writer Drew Goddard  were brought in to offer tweaks to  Carnahan script what they eventually  delivered was an all-out expensive  redesign of the film's third act which  Paramount agreed the fund the film's  budget ballooned to at least 190 million  dollars and by the end of the shoot  Forrester and Pitt were reportedly not  on speaking terms anymore so after all  this back and forth where did we wind up  instead of crash landing in Russia  Lane's zombie-infested fight out of  Israel heads for a World Health  Organization facility in Wales as it's  coming in for a landing however the  zombies threatened to overrun everything  Lane and either a really brilliant or  really dumb move detonates a grenade  that tears a hole in the fuselage and  depressurizes the cabin leading to all  the zombies being sucked out and the  plane coming in for an intense crash  landing after a blackout Lane impaled by  a rather large piece of shrapnel wakes  up in the wreckage and tries to make his  way to the w-h-o outpost that was his  initial destination overcome by his  injuries he loses consciousness and  later awakes under the care of a w-h-o  doctor played by a future doctor who  star Peter Capaldi after regaining his  senses he comes to a shocking conclusion  having seen the zombie horde passed by  the sick and elderly he believes that  the virus drives its host to seek out  only healthy and viable victims to  facilitate its spread if this be the key  to humanity's survival wouldn't you 